#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Summarize measured legacy improvements and explicitly retained gaps."""
import json,statistics
from pathlib import Path
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];OUT=ROOT/'reports/multiformat-legacy-layout-2026-11-12'
def read(p):return json.loads(p.read_text())
def main():
 s=read(OUT/'benchmark-final/summary.json');q=read(OUT/'quality-results.json');env=read(OUT/'benchmark-final/environment.json');c=read(OUT/'change-summary.json');v=read(OUT/'validation/summary.json');audit=read(OUT/'output-change-review.json');prev=read(ROOT/'reports/multiformat-tables-layout-2026-11-12/benchmark-final/summary.json')
 old={k:sum(x[k] for name,x in q['cohorts'].items() if not name.startswith('legacy_')) for k in ['before','after','anydoc','checks']}
 lines=['# Legacy layout and formatting — 12 November 2026','',
 '**Eight legacy outputs improve using BulkParse-owned general rules.** The 81-document conversion corpus is unchanged. Word now reads table-style records without losing unrelated text formatting, applies character-style overrides, and reconstructs table rows/merges from physical boundaries. Legacy PowerPoint reads local and per-slide master formatting, including nested bullets. RTF preserves escaped line endings and keeps list-label formatting from overwriting heading roles.','',
 '## Quality and remaining gaps','',
 '| Selected source-grounded checks | BulkParse before | BulkParse after | AnyDoc |','| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |']
 for name,r in [('Previous checks, unchanged',old),('New legacy formatting/layout',q['cohorts']['legacy_fixes']),('Explicit legacy table spans',q['cohorts']['legacy_structure']),('Remaining legacy gaps',q['cohorts']['legacy_remaining'])]:lines.append(f"| {name} | {r['before']}/{r['checks']} | {r['after']}/{r['checks']} | {r['anydoc']}/{r['checks']} |")
 lines += [f"| Total | {q['totals']['before']}/{q['checks']} | {q['totals']['after']}/{q['checks']} | {q['totals']['anydoc']}/{q['checks']} |",'',
 '**These are development expectations, not a whole-document quality percentage or an independent holdout.** The previous 69 predicates are unchanged. Twelve newly checked gaps are fixed. Four known gaps are intentionally included and still fail: Word automatic numbering, RTF note bodies, structural RTF bullets, and legacy PPT table reconstruction. AnyDoc passes the first three and also flattens the PPT table. The explicit Word-span check requires actual merged-table structure; AnyDoc’s expanded Markdown retains cell placement but not spans. These output-model differences limit aggregate comparisons.','',
 f"All **{c['returned']}/{c['conversion_documents']} inputs** return output; **{c['changed_outputs']} predictions change**. Status remains **{c['statuses']['partial']} partial / {c['statuses']['complete']} complete**. The two Word `doc_style_metadata` failures are resolved, but broad diagnostics for remaining document features still apply. A partial flag is not a measured fraction of missing content, and complete status does not prove perfect fidelity.",'',
 'The audit covers all 62 baseline partial documents. The legacy subset contains 25 DOC/PPT/RTF/XLS/XLSB conversion inputs, 21 of which remain partial. The eight changed outputs are three DOC, three PPT and two RTF documents. Legacy XLS/XLSB formatting and visibility limitations are unchanged; the fixes here target verified DOC/PPT/RTF defects.','',
 '### Root causes and implementation','',
 '- **Word style families:** STSH family-4 table-style UPX payloads were wrongly interpreted as character-property instructions. Their valid binary data caused a parse error, which discarded all optional formatting. Paragraph and character payloads are now interpreted only for their respective families; opaque table/numbering styles no longer invalidate them. This restores localized headings, captions, quotes and emphasis without matching document text or filenames.',
 '- **Word character overrides:** `sprmCIstd` resolves the referenced character style before direct formatting. Toggle values use the style base, so repeated relative toggles do not accidentally toggle against each other. Variable-length table operands use the specified two-byte size, keeping following instructions aligned.',
 '- **Word tables:** cell/row terminators are interpreted with PAPX table flags. `TDefTable` boundaries, TC80 merge flags and row-header flags feed the existing shared edge-based table builder. Rich cell paragraphs and covered-cell text stay in the anchor. One bounded Data-stream huge-PAPX indirection is supported. Nested tables and arbitrary later table mutations remain incomplete. Malformed optional property records are diagnosed and fall back to retained text; resource limits or inconsistent assembled geometry can still reject a document.',
 '- **Legacy PowerPoint:** text bodies collect their associated `StyleTextPropAtom` before emission. Paragraph/character runs use UTF-16 positions, including supplementary characters and the implicit final mark. Active slide master IDs select per-level defaults; explicit local off/on bits override inheritance. Bullet depths become nested lists, and soft line breaks remain inline. Invalid optional style records produce diagnostics and retain the text; resource-limit/cancellation errors still propagate. Notes retain their existing slide ownership.',
 '- **RTF paragraphs:** a backslash followed by LF, CR or CRLF ends a paragraph once; raw physical newlines remain insignificant. Within a table it becomes an inline break. Paragraph role is captured outside label-local `pard`/`plain` resets, so headings remain headings even when labels contain only a tab. No automatic list reconstruction was added.',
 '- Production rules use binary record families, properties, run lengths and relationship IDs. No benchmark paths, fixture strings or document identities are used by the implementation. AnyDoc remains a comparator/design reference, not a runtime dependency.','',
 f"The [changed-output review](output-change-review.json) and [full diff](output-change-review.diff) cover all eight predictions. Their normalized alphanumeric content and order are unchanged; formatting and cell grouping improve. All **{len(audit['html_tables'])} emitted HTML tables** pass rectangular-occupancy checks. These guards do not establish punctuation fidelity or semantic correctness of every cell.",'',
 '### Still incomplete','',
 '- Word list numbering/restarts, auxiliary notes, links/anchors, floating objects, nested tables and the full character/table property language.',
 '- PPT physical table geometry and spatial reading order, advanced numbering, full font/theme effects and images. Numbered paragraphs can remain bullets because extended numbering properties are not reconstructed.',
 '- RTF automatic numbering/list structure, nested tables, note/header/footer stories and full links/embedded objects. Literal labels are still retained.',
 '- Legacy XLS/XLSB full rich styles, visibility/display rules, links, drawings and advanced records.',
 '- The existing default Node optimizing-WASM compiler problem on larger PDFs remains unresolved; Linux/browser testing remains outstanding.','',
 '## Same-machine benchmark','',
 f"Machine: **{env['machine']}**, {env['platform']}. BulkParse {env['versions']['bulkparse']} (schema **0.5**), AnyDoc {env['versions']['anydoc']}, Docling {env['versions']['docling']}. The same 70 upstream fixtures plus 11 authored conversion inputs are used; nine robustness inputs run separately.",'',
 '| Engine | Returned / attempted | Median sequential full-corpus time | Lifetime peak RSS |','| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |']
 for e,r in s['engines'].items():lines.append(f"| {e} | {r['returned']}/{r['attempted']} | {r['median_corpus_ms']:.3f} ms | {s['resources'][e]['lifetime_peak_rss_bytes']/1048576:.1f} MiB |")
 runs={e:[read(OUT/f'benchmark-final/{e}-pass-{i}.json')['documents'] for i in range(1,6)] for e in s['engines']};common=set.intersection(*[{r['path'] for r in val[0] if r['ok']} for val in runs.values()]);times={e:statistics.median(sum(r['elapsed_ns'] for r in run if r['path'] in common)/1e6 for run in val) for e,val in runs.items()}
 lines += ['',
 'BulkParse and AnyDoc process the identical 81 inputs. Docling attempts only the same 31 supported OOXML fixtures; its six existing synthetic PPTX failures remain in the attempted-corpus timings. It does not directly benchmark these legacy DOC/PPT/RTF changes. On the same '+str(len(common))+' successful inputs across all three, medians are '+', '.join(f'{e} **{t:.3f} ms**' for e,t in times.items())+'.','',
 'One excluded full warm-up precedes five full-corpus runs with rotating engine order. Persistent workers convert sequentially with thread settings of one. Timings include reads, parsing and default Markdown export, excluding process startup, IPC, output serialization/writes and quality scoring. Corpus clocks sum the per-document measurements. Five-pass outputs/outcomes are deterministic. Memory is macOS lifetime peak RSS, including warm-up and the Rust workers’ separate robustness inputs; it is not per-document incremental memory. Raw CPU totals include startup.','',
 f"Previous BulkParse corpus median: **{prev['engines']['bulkparse']['median_corpus_ms']:.3f} ms**; current: **{s['engines']['bulkparse']['median_corpus_ms']:.3f} ms**. Current BulkParse time is **{s['engines']['bulkparse']['median_corpus_ms']/s['engines']['anydoc']['median_corpus_ms']:.3f}× AnyDoc’s**. Old/new comparisons use separate runs, not interleaved binaries. More extracted formatting changes the work performed. These small macOS fixtures do not establish Linux production throughput.",'',
 '| Format | Inputs | BulkParse median document ms | AnyDoc median document ms | BulkParse partial |','| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |']
 for fmt,eng in s['per_format'].items():
  b=eng['bulkparse'];a=eng['anydoc'];lines.append(f"| {fmt.upper()} | {b['attempted']} | {b['median_document_ms']:.3f} | {a['median_document_ms']:.3f} | {b['partial']} |")
 lines += ['', 'Per-document medians use the five measurements for each input, then aggregate by extension. Unsupported formats are not timed for Docling; attempted failures remain included.','',
 '## Validation and references','',
 f"- **{v['rust_all_tests']} all-feature Rust workspace tests pass**, including **47 Office integration tests**. Minimal core: **{v['rust_minimal_tests']}**; Office-only: **{v['rust_office_tests']}**. Clippy with warnings denied and formatting checks pass.",
 '- Eight new tests cover non-character Word style payloads, relative toggles, variable-length operands, physical Word table edges/merges and limits, PPT supplementary-character run offsets, master overrides, nested bullets and malformed style fallback, RTF line endings and label-local resets.',
 '- Node/Python each pass four smoke tests; WASM smoke tests pass. Parity covers **34 conversions + three inspections** across Node/Python/WASM/CLI, including all eight changed predictions and the previous changed-table corpus. Extended parity covers **41 conversions + three inspections** using `node --liftoff-only`.',
 '- The default Node 24 optimizing-compiler OOM on larger PDF/WASM inputs remains a known limitation; the extended check uses the previously documented workaround.',
 '- All **200 PDF Markdown predictions remain byte-for-byte unchanged**, using the benchmarked binary. PDF metric evaluation and speed were not rerun for these Office changes.',
 '- The 11 authored semantic checks remain passing for BulkParse and AnyDoc; Docling passes its two supported authored checks. All nine robustness accept/reject outcomes remain unchanged; recovered outputs are compared separately in validation evidence.',
 '- [Validation logs and summary](validation/summary.json), [PDF equality](pdf-regression.json), [robustness comparison](validation/robustness-comparison.json).','',
 'Design review used AnyDoc’s Word SPRM/style, PPT run/master and RTF lexer modules. [Exact local reference hashes](design-reference-hashes.json) and [license notices](../../THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md) are retained. Binary interpretation was checked against Microsoft’s [Word table operand](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/openspecs/office_file_formats/ms-doc/de06ec41-a0ac-4046-9096-cdfaa0091ad9), [PowerPoint character formatting](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/openspecs/office_file_formats/ms-ppt/c75024a2-14cb-4d7d-9964-bdab2fcd9d93) and [PowerPoint text-body boundaries](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/openspecs/office_file_formats/ms-ppt/08d31a66-0750-4009-b416-49f2871cd178).','',
 '## Reproduce and download','',
 'Restore the hash-matched corpora and comparator environments described in the [multiformat protocol](../../benchmarks/multiformat/README.md).','',
 '```sh','cargo test --workspace --all-features','cargo build --release -p bulkparse --example office_bench','python3 scripts/benchmark_office_formats.py --out reports/my-legacy-layout-run','python3 scripts/validate_office_benchmark.py reports/my-legacy-layout-run','python3 scripts/evaluate_office_quality.py --run reports/my-legacy-layout-run \\','  --baseline reports/multiformat-tables-layout-2026-11-12/benchmark-final \\','  --spec reports/multiformat-legacy-layout-2026-11-12/quality-checks.json \\','  --out reports/my-legacy-layout-evaluation','python3 scripts/audit_legacy_layout_outputs.py --run reports/my-legacy-layout-run \\','  --out reports/my-legacy-layout-evaluation/output-change-review.json','python3 scripts/check_office_pdf_regression.py --out reports/my-legacy-layout-evaluation/pdf-regression.json','```','',
 '- [Download source and evidence ZIP](../multiformat-legacy-layout-2026-11-12.zip); upstream documents, dependencies and compiled binaries are excluded.',
 '- [Benchmark summary](benchmark-final/summary.json), [environment/binary hashes](benchmark-final/environment.json), [corpus manifest](benchmark-final/manifest.json), [source hashes](benchmark-final/source-manifest.json).',
 '- [Quality manifest](quality-checks.json), [all outcomes](quality-results.json), [62-document audit](partial-audit.md), [previous report](../multiformat-tables-layout-2026-11-12/README.md).',
 '- Raw warm-up/five-pass predictions, resource logs and robustness results are under `benchmark-final`; `before-source` and `source-snapshot` preserve prior/final implementation.','']
 (OUT/'README.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines))
if __name__=='__main__':main()
